"}]}

{"id": "4961205c-a764-4ac0-86b8-f627118652fe", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll look through CloudTrail for the bucket deletion and find the principal. This covers the past couple of weeks, so a deletion last week is included.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_v7qPiKBp8QU2PA58qj93Gz", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "s3-bucket-delete-lookup", "agent_type": "generic", "preloaded_skills": ["investigating-infrastructure-changes"], "prompt": "{
  "task": "Find the CloudTrail event where the S3 bucket 'nebula-ct-gap-logs' was deleted, and identify the principal who did it.",
  "context": "User asks 'Who deleted the S3 bucket nebula-ct-gap-logs last week?'. Current date is 2026-11-19 (Thursday). 'Last week' is likely Nov 9-15, 2026, but search a wider window to be safe. The agent space is in account 012345678901 (us-east-1); the bucket may live in this account or another associated account, and could be in any region. This is a bounded lookup, not a root-cause hunt.",
  "resources": ["S3 bucket: nebula-ct-gap-logs", "event names: DeleteBucket (also check DeleteBucketPolicy, PutBucketLifecycle*, DeleteObject/DeleteObjects only if data events exist, and any lifecycle-based emptying)"],
  "timeframe": "2026-11-08T00:00:00Z/2026-11-19T15:40:00Z",
  "criteria": "Look up events by ResourceName=nebula-ct-gap-logs and by EventName=DeleteBucket. Check us-east-1 first, then other regions if nothing is found. Also check other associated accounts if there are any. Report: event time (UTC), eventName, eventID, awsRegion, account, userIdentity (type, ARN, principalId, userName, and for assumed roles the session name and the underlying role/SSO user or federated identity if resolvable), sourceIPAddress, userAgent, any errorCode (distinguish a successful delete from a failed or denied attempt), and the request parameters. If no event is found, state exactly which regions, accounts and time windows were searched and what could explain the gap (event outside the lookup window, bucket in another account or region, deletion done by an AWS service or lifecycle, etc.). Do not guess the principal; only report what the event shows."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Search CloudTrail for S3 bucket deletion event"}], "created_at": null}

